{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CguzuSiCF28VtmFnBxPut","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I read the code, the roadmap, the ADR and the draft specs, but couldn't run any tool or test. My session refused every command, including the plan's own `pose` tools. So every tool and criterion below rests on the sealed evidence plus my reading of the code, not on a run of mine.\n\ndecision: approved\n\n## Round-1 findings\n\n| ID | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1-F1 (medium) | **fixed** | The memo key now includes a digest of `git config --list -z --includes`, which covers every Git config scope. It is read once per operation (`governance_read_view_git.go:55-69`), passed in at `:363` and added to the key at `resident_git_memo.go:86`. If the config can't be read, nothing is cached (`:63-66`). A test covers a change to the user's config file (`resident_git_memo_test.go:120-153`). Requirement R2 of draft spec `pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key` is withdrawn to match. |\n| R1-F2 (low) | **not fixed, still a follow-up** | `runtime_host.go:134,145` still compute `memo_hits` from the global counter. It's tracked as R1 of draft spec `pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key`. |\n| R1-F3 (low) | **fixed** | ADR line 5 now reads \"Accepted for the delivered scope\" and lists what was and wasn't delivered (lines 5-13). |\n| R1-F4 (low) | **fixed** | `pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md:37-38`: R2 adds CPU affinity and `io.max`, and R4 measures I/O. |\n\n## New findings (both low, follow-ups)\n\n- **N1**: `.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:298` describes the old memo key: commit, shallow file and repository config. It doesn't mention the effective config digest.\n- **N2**: `pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go:18-19` has the same outdated wording in the comment above `ResidentGitMemo` (\"the key holds the commit and the shallow state\").\n\n## Criteria\n\nAll seven are judged **passed** on sealed evidence plus my reading of the code. Details are in the draft. The four not-delivered items in the roadmap's status paragraph are each in a spec of their own, all with `status: draft`:\n- `pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command`\n- `pose-runtime-windows-named-pipe`\n- `pose-checks-route-to-the-runtime-by-default`\n- `pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key`\n\n## Points to check before recording\n\n- **No tool run of mine.** `roadmap-check` and `validate` for pose-mcp are declared `passed` on sealed refs, as the implementer's notes instruct. I didn't run them.\n- **`validate` for scripts.** It's `not-used` because the notes say the plan marks it `producer_coverage none`. I couldn't see the plan to confirm that. The sealed evidence has no scripts refs, which is consistent with it.\n- **Owner and dates.** I put the git user name as owner and 2026-12-10 as `review_by` on the follow-ups. Change either if they're wrong.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\", \"line\": 298, \"summary\": \"The ADR amendment's Caches bullet says the resident memo is keyed by the commit, the shallow file and the repository config; the key now holds the digest of the effective Git configuration of every scope (resident_git_memo.go:86, governance_read_view_git.go:55).\", \"action\": \"Update the Caches bullet to name the effective Git configuration digest as part of the key\", \"owner\": \"Oseias Pereira\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\", \"line\": 18, \"summary\": \"The ResidentGitMemo doc comment still says the key holds the commit and the shallow state; it omits the effective Git configuration digest that the key now includes (line 86).\", \"action\": \"Update the doc comment to list the configuration digest as part of the key\", \"owner\": \"Oseias Pereira\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go:55-69 digests `git config --list -z --includes` once per operation per root; :363 passes it to residentGitKey; resident_git_memo.go:62-66,86 puts it in the key and memoizes nothing when it is unreadable; resident_git_memo_test.go:120-153 shows a user-config change alters the digest across operations; draft spec pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key R2 withdrawn accordingly.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F2\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:134,145 still take memo_hits as the difference of the global ResidentGitMemoStats counter; still a low follow-up tracked as R1 of draft spec .pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md:36.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:5-13 status reads 'Accepted for the delivered scope — 2026-11-10' and lists delivered and not-adopted items.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F4\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md:37-38: R2 covers CPU affinity and an I/O limit (io.max), and R4 measures I/O under the limit.\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Read the roadmap .pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md (outcome, Estado paragraph, four milestones and exit gates), the ADR status and 2026-11-10 amendment (lines 1-13, 275-313), the resident memo (resident_git_memo.go), the config digest and memo use in the governance Git capture (governance_read_view_git.go:1-110, 300-420), the pure-read classifier (governance_git_pure.go) and gitCommandContext env handling, the hosted handler 